{"id": "EUVD-2026-108423", "enisaUuid": "3cfd9613-225f-3c52-aa34-0a8c61e3ff4f", "description": "Mistune before 3.3.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the opt-in Include directive that allows attackers to read local files by supplying relative or absolute include paths. Attackers who submit Markdown rendered via Markdown.read() can disclose files such as /etc/passwd and inject unescaped HTML or script content into rendered output.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/lepture/mistune/security/advisories/GHSA-jhcm-5rpf-j3wv", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mistune-before-3.3.0-arbitrary-local-file-read-via-include-directive"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115354", "GHSA-r6px-88r6-4rqg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f60c135a-48a8-3ee5-93d8-f5b72e99966b", "product": {"name": "mistune", "vendor": {"name": "lepture"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "120ebd94-22ef-3a06-b86a-cc9ecf1cf7cb", "vendor": {"name": "lepture"}}], "isExploited": false}